<%- include('partials/head', { title: 'Pulseboard — real-time retro & kanban' }) %>
<header class="topbar">
  <div class="wrap">
    <a class="brand" href="/"><span class="brand-dot"></span> Pulseboard</a>
    <span class="spacer"></span>
    <a class="btn btn-sm" href="https://github.com/<%= process.env.GITHUB_REPO || '0211IkeVenLouie/pulseboard' %>">Source ↗</a>
  </div>
</header>

<main class="wrap narrow">
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Boards that move <span class="gradient-text">while you watch</span>.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Open the same link in two windows and drag a card. It lands in both — cursors,
      votes and all. No accounts, no email, no invite flow. The URL is the room.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="<%= demoSlug ? '/b/' + demoSlug : '/demo' %>">Open the demo board →</a>
      <a class="btn" href="#new">Start an empty board</a>
    </div>
    <div class="chips">
      <span class="chip" style="--chip-hue: var(--hue-1)">Live cursors</span>
      <span class="chip" style="--chip-hue: var(--hue-2)">Retro voting</span>
      <span class="chip" style="--chip-hue: var(--hue-3)">Hide until reveal</span>
      <span class="chip" style="--chip-hue: var(--hue-4)">No signup</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="new">
    <div class="card">
      <h2>New board</h2>
      <form method="post" action="/boards">
        <div class="field">
          <label for="title">Board name</label>
          <input type="text" id="title" name="title" placeholder="Sprint 24 retro" maxlength="120" />
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="kind">Template</label>
          <select id="kind" name="kind">
            <option value="retro">Retro — Went well / To improve / Action items</option>
            <option value="kanban">Kanban — Backlog / In progress / Review / Done</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Create board</button>
        <p class="hint">Anyone with the link can read and edit. Boards are not listed anywhere.</p>
      </form>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <p class="section-label">What is actually hard here</p>
    <h2>Two people drag the same card at the same moment.</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      Most implementations answer “last write wins”, which means one person’s drag
      silently undoes the other’s while both screens show something different.
    </p>

    <div class="split" style="margin-top: 18px;">
      <div class="feature">
        <div class="feature-icon">⇅</div>
        <h3>Fractional ordering</h3>
        <p>A card’s position is a string, not an integer, so a move rewrites one row instead of renumbering a whole column.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature">
        <div class="feature-icon">⚔</div>
        <h3>Version guards</h3>
        <p>A stale drag is rejected with the authoritative card, and the optimistic UI snaps back instead of undoing someone else's move.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature">
        <div class="feature-icon">▲</div>
        <h3>Votes commute</h3>
        <p>Two people voting at once is not a conflict, it is two votes — so votes skip the guard entirely.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature">
        <div class="feature-icon">◐</div>
        <h3>Masked server-side</h3>
        <p>Hidden retro cards never reach another browser. Masking in CSS is one devtools inspection from useless.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="muted" style="margin-top: 18px;">
      <a href="https://github.com/<%= process.env.GITHUB_REPO || '0211IkeVenLouie/pulseboard' %>#the-hard-part">Read the full write-up →</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</main>

<footer class="site wrap"><span class="faint">Pulseboard · Node, Postgres, Socket.IO</span></footer>
</body>
</html>
